2026-10-10T04:13:02Z  NOTE      fix: the renderer per-tick PCM batch is sized from the rate the audio queue actually carries — AudioQueue publishes the last pushed rate (a relaxed atomic stored in pushAll, read off the audio thread at worst one push stale) and renderFrame uses the pure framesPerRenderTick(queueRate, targetFps, buffer) — replacing the hardcoded audioSampleRate_=48000 member, which is deleted. A 44.1 kHz sink is no longer batch-sized as 48 kHz (~9% misfeed -> beat-detection drift).
2026-10-10T04:13:02Z  NOTE      bonus defect fixed in the same expression, disclosed: the old sizer (48000 + fps - 1)/fps could exceed the 4096-frame pop buffer at low fps — the config clamp floor is 10 fps, where 48 kHz asks for 4800 frames -> popVizBatch would write 9600 floats into an 8192-float stack buffer. framesPerRenderTick clamps to the buffer; the clamp is load-bearing and pinned by the new test. The overflow was reachable today at fps=10.
2026-10-10T04:13:02Z  NOTE      the queue default 48000 survives only until the first push; AudioEngine pushes the OBSERVED sink rate (T0153 board evidence), so the renderer follows reality. T0153 (recorder resampler in_rate) remains its own task — the queue now carries the shared truth it needs. Tests: test_Playlist theQueueCarriesThePushedSampleRate (default + 44.1k push); test_ProjectMFramebuffer batchSizingFollowsTheQueuesRateAndClampsToThePopBuffer (pure helper: 44.1k@60fps=735, 48k@60fps=800, both clamped to 4096 at 10fps).
2026-10-10T04:13:02Z  VERIFY    ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests --output-on-failure -j"$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)" => "100% tests passed out of 13" (unit_tests 64.14s, 2026-10-09 local); both new tests PASS by direct suite proof. Caveat: audible beat-sync is runtime behaviour — machine evidence is the batch-math pinned per rate and the queue carrying the pushed rate; a human on a screen can watch beat detection on a 44.1 kHz sink.
